WEBVTT

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.200
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.290
Sometimes, as you walk down a busy street,

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:28.620
you encounter a vacuum--
a place with no air whatsoever.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.620
Someone lost their life,

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:35.870
and someone who cared about them
left behind some white flowers.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:41.500
What would you do if the one who
died there was irreplaceable for you?

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.080
This is a story about a funny old man
for whom I harbor heartfelt pride.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.250
"Ikebukuro West Gate Park"

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.290
Free tissues!

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.410
"...searching for whoever...
...24 around 7PM...
...manslaughter was committed here."

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.830
Excuse me.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.160
Do you pass by here often?

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:37.620
Huh?

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:38.200
"...searching for whoever... ...24 around 7PM...
...manslaughter was committed here."

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:38.200
Huh?

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.330
"...searching for whoever... ...24 around 7PM...
...manslaughter was committed here."
Do you remember what you were
doing at that time, and where?

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.250
Do you remember what you were
doing at that time, and where?

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.120
Here.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.830
Oh, thanks.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:53.660
If my Toshi was alive now,
he'd be about your age.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:57.370
And if my old man was alive,
he'd be about yours.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:03.540
He was my only son.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.080
He had a bit of a reputation in Ueno.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:10.620
He was the leader of some
sort of street gang, I guess.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.000
He was rowdy, maybe because
I raised him on my own.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.120
But he also had a kind side.
He took care of his guys.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.160
It was five years ago today.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.040
I was suddenly told to come to the hospital,

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.040
and there was Toshi, already turning cold.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:33.290
He was a hotheaded guy, so maybe
he got into a scuffle with some punk.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:37.700
Hey, do you know any gang members or punks?

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.580
I'd like you to see if you
can casually get any info.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.500
Sure. My situation's kind of similar.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.700
I'll try asking around.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.790
Thank you.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.200
Grandpa!

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.250
Oh, there you are!

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.450
Akihiro, this guy's name is Makoto.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:57.910
Say hello.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.370
I'm Akihiro Matsuda, age four!

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:03.830
My favorite foods are apples, melons, and fruit!

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:07.790
That's perfect. We sell fruit at my place.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.540
Next time, I'll give you
a bunch of unsold stuff.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:15.540
Thank you for listening to his grandpa's story.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.080
I'm Harumi, Akihiro's mother.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.700
Oh, sure thing.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.330
I'm Makoto Majima.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.580
Big Sis Harumi! It's been forever!

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:28.540
Keep your voice down. I'm not
involved with the Team anymore.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.290
Number two's not with you today?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.660
That's right. Kouji-san is at work.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.620
Well, Dad. We're going to go.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.660
Already? I'll join you!

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.450
No, I've got an errand to run.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:59.120
Oh, yeah? I'll bring Akihiro's
Christmas present by later.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.250
Now, Makoto. Where do you live?

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.290
I'll drive you home.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:08.370
Oh, it's really close. I don't need a ride.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:12.160
Just humor me. You can fit in at least one song.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.330
Song?

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.370
You've never heard of a jazz taxi?

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.580
I've never been in a taxi like <i>this</i>.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.660
Here.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:26.790
Choose which one you want.
It'll be the BGM for tonight's drive.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:28.370
Okay, this one.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:31.950
"Night Train," is it? You've got
good taste for one so young.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:34.200
"Radio"   "Video"     "Settings"      "Navigation"

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:34.200
"Night Train," is it? You've got
good taste for one so young.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.700
"Takashi"

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.830
Takashi, is this about what I asked you?

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:17.580
I had a dozen G-Boys go ask around,
but they found nothing.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.330
I checked with former members, too,

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.450
but nobody knew about
any murders from five years ago.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:25.700
Okay. Thanks for checking around.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:28.450
I did find some other info, though,
about a "Team" in Ueno.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.540
"Miki no Kashi"

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.540
I did find some other info, though,
about a "Team" in Ueno.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:38.620
Toshi of Ame-Yoko is famous for putting
together an Ueno gang called Team Apollo.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:42.290
Apparently, they're on their
third leader now--name of Rintarou.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.790
"Gumbo"

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.950
I'll have a dark beer.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.200
I'm writing a column for a fashion magazine.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:07.790
Is there anyone who could tell me
about the late Toshi-san?

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:14.080
I also know his old man, Yasuhiro Nanjou-san.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.160
If I can get an interview,
I'd love to do the story justice.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.870
You won't get any help here.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.620
Don't go digging up the past.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:29.950
Is that how all of Ueno's Team
feels, not just you?

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.120
We don't plan on telling you a thing.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:35.870
Finish your beer, then get out of here.

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:40.450
It's all yours.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.620
Okay, got it. Thanks.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.000
Looks like I'm finally going to hear the story.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.750
What are we supposed to tell you?

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.750
You've been banned from this town.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:26.370
I don't think so. I'm not on some fool's errand.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:27.870
Asshole!

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.160
Get him!

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:36.580
A fight?

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.200
We'd better call the police.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.830
Never come to Ueno again.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:47.290
Next time you show your face here,
it'll go down the same as today.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:50.120
All of Apollo stands behind that.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.120
Oww...

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.370
"Majima Produce"

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.200
"Majima Produce"

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.200
Makoto! A man named Nanjou-san
is here to see you!

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.750
Makoto! A man named Nanjou-san
is here to see you!

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.200
What happened, Makoto?!

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.120
Oh, this happens all the time.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:10.580
He can take it, he's tough. No need to worry.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:12.660
I got beat up in Ueno.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.540
Today I'm going to go talk to Apollo's leader.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.160
What do you mean?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.750
It looks like they're hiding
something about Toshi-san.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.330
You never learn.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:28.870
I'm not here by myself today.
I brought Toshi-san's old man with me.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:32.870
I know Apollo is hiding
something about Toshi-san.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:37.540
If you insist that you don't want
to tell me, I'll bring his dad up here.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.660
What'll it be?

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:44.330
You don't know anything.
That's why you can be so drastic.

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:48.370
I don't plan on giving up until
I find out that thing I don't know.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.580
Your face looks awful.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:57.160
It's true. Some people do some awful things.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.040
Okay, then. I'll get in touch with our boss.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.580
You're the head of Apollo?

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:12.040
I'm Rintarou Nagai,
the third-generation head of Apollo.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:14.120
Sorry to trouble you.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:20.040
But I have to know what it is
you guys are hiding about Toshi-san.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:24.160
What have you heard about
Toshi-san from his old man?

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:27.580
That he raised him alone, and he's proud of him.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.120
And that he had a kind side.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:33.080
Is that not true?

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:34.500
It's true.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:39.580
But that was limited just
to Toshi-san's favorite members.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:42.290
You never knew what he might do
when he snapped.

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:45.250
After the incident, Harumi-san's
current husband, Kouji-san

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:49.410
became our second leader.
Toshi-san was harsh with him, too.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:53.580
Despite all that, he was highly
considerate when he <i>was </i>nice.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:11:00.080
When my sister was hospitalized,
he was first to visit, and he brought flowers.

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:03.000
Everyone's like that, sometimes.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.830
You don't hit women, do you?

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:07.830
Did Toshi-san used to hit them?

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:14.120
Yeah. Harumi-san, who lived
with him, got it especially bad.

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.870
Apollo was strong back then,

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:20.160
but it was Kouji-san who
later made it as huge as it is.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:23.450
If the incident hadn't happened,
and Toshi-san had remained our boss,

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:26.160
I'm sure Apollo would have fallen apart.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.700
That's all I can tell you.

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:36.910
If there's anything else you must know,
ask Harumi-san firsthand.

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:42.000
But listen, be very careful
when you tell the old man.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:46.330
There's really no need
to go hurting his dead son.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:51.040
"Episode 4"

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:58.410
They say children are innocent,
and it sure is true.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:02.200
Even Toshi was that age, once.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:05.660
Before I knew it, he was
in a gang, of all things.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:10.040
Makoto, you'd better not go
and make your mother cry.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.290
She's the one who makes <i>me </i>cry.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.950
"Sukoyaka
Kindergarten"

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.540
Sorry for springing this on you.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.330
I've already heard nearly
everything from leader #3.

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:24.410
There's just one more thing
I want to check on. All right?

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:29.330
Akihiro is leader #2--Kouji-san's kid, isn't he?

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:31.040
Look, Grandpa! Look!

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:34.080
Oh, what a big leaf!

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:39.000
Yes. He's Kouji-san's boy.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:44.580
I always got hit, and when Kouji-san
stood up for me, he got hit, too.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:49.450
We were in the same situation,
so we talked, and comforted each other.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.160
It wasn't long before we were
meeting without Toshi's knowledge.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.950
Hey, what will you do?

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:58.790
Do you plan to tell Grandpa Nanjou?

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:02.040
No, I'll find some way to keep it from him.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:05.950
Nobody really needs to know the full story.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:12.290
Sometimes, though, I just don't know.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:18.750
I feel like telling him everything,
especially when he dotes on Akihiro.

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:27.790
If there's still something
bugging you, why not tell me?

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.790
How would you understand?!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:33.450
I'm going to live with this
secret the rest of my life!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.660
It's not so simple, like something
you just write about!

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:41.160
There's no deadline, no end.
Just one long, shitty life!

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:52.200
On that day five years ago, I told Toshi.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:55.290
That I wanted to break up.
That I loved someone else.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.830
Then, Toshi lost his temper again.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:02.330
But no matter how much he hit me,
I did all I could to protect my belly.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:09.580
At one point he noticed, and he
asked me why I was shielding it.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:12.250
I told him I was pregnant.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:16.660
And that the child inside me wasn't his.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:19.410
What did Toshihiro do then?

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:22.500
He ran out of my apartment.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:28.160
His face looked so cold then,
I got worried and followed him.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:32.910
We had promised to go to Ikebukuro
for Christmas, so I thought he might be there.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.950
When Toshi was confirmed dead at the hospital,

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:54.450
I was shocked, but extremely
relieved at the same time.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:59.910
I thought, at least Toshi wouldn't
go and kill Kouji-san.

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:10.290
Harumi-san, the other day...

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:11.700
Misako-san!

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:13.700
Thanks for the other day.

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:15.910
Is he a family member of yours?

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:17.750
Uh, no...

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:21.500
Majima-san is someone Grandpa Nanjou knows.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:25.540
Harumi-san.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:29.580
Five years ago, you discovered
Toshi-san lying on the ground.

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:32.250
Didn't you see something else, at the time?

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:34.330
No, I don't think so.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:38.290
It was five years ago, so I've forgotten.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:41.120
Makoto-san, you've done enough.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.870
You know what kind of person Toshi was.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:47.250
Misako-san, I've got to go.
There's so much to do today.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.620
Makoto?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.040
If you want to have a drink, that's a no,

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:06.540
because I have a date tonight
with one hottie of a judicial trainee.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:09.660
Sorry, could you just give me five minutes?

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.750
I want you to check on someone
in some old case files.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:13.950
What case?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:17.410
A murder case from five years ago,
behind Metropolitan Theater.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.870
I want to know the testimony
of the first woman on the scene.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:25.080
You're poking your nose into
some troublesome affairs again.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.580
All right, hold on a minute.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:33.120
You owe me one for this, okay?

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:36.370
Looks like I'll be 15 minutes late
for my date, thanks to you.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:39.450
All right. Next time, it's my treat.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:43.200
You sound down. You okay, Makoto?

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:49.660
Here goes. The first on
the scene was Harumi Ueda.

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:52.290
A 21-year-old common-law wife.

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:56.200
She testified that where the victim was
lying on the stairs behind the theater,

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:59.540
she saw a young couple fleeing the scene.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.370
The man's height was about 175cm.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:07.580
The woman was tall, around 170cm.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.330
That's about it.

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:13.080
Have you obtained some
info linked to the killer?

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:15.000
No, never mind.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.370
Looks like I had the wrong idea.

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:20.200
You go and enjoy your date. See ya.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:21.410
Hey, Mako--

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.160
"Majima Produce"

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.620
Makoto?

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:34.620
I'm going to meet with Nanjou-san next week.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:35.910
What will you do?

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:38.000
You don't need to worry.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:41.910
I'll feed him a story that's plausible.

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:47.540
Let him go on being a good
grandpa to Akihiro from now on.

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:48.700
Thank you.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:52.200
Once the new year starts,
I'll bring by some fruit from my place.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.500
Bye.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:12.000
Makoto, thanks for everything.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.580
I couldn't accomplish anything, in the end.

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:19.290
And all I've got to show for it
is this busted-up face.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:25.080
I've heard a number of bad
rumors about Toshi, myself.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:30.500
But, whatever! I have faith in you, Makoto.

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:33.160
Excuse us!

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:39.660
My name is Misako Matsuoka.

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:50.700
I'm sorry. I was the one who pushed
Toshihiro-san down the steps that night.

00:18:54.950 --> 00:19:00.750
This doesn't make sense.
Explain it to me from the beginning.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:06.250
That night, I talked to Toshi about breaking up.

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:11.790
I was too ashamed to tell you,
but Toshi was terrible at home.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:14.410
He would always hit me.

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:18.870
I had bruises on me all year round.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:23.700
But even so, I was too scared to leave him.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:27.910
And then I found someone I truly loved.

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:30.580
You mean Kouji-san?

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.330
Yes.

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:39.330
I see...

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:44.080
I'm sorry my idiot son did such a thing.

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:50.370
Akihiro is still Toshi's son, isn't he?

00:19:57.080 --> 00:20:02.250
Akihiro... Akihiro was never my grandson...

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:06.700
I see...

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:12.580
And you, Miss. Why did you push Toshi?

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:17.200
I was on my way home from a date
with my husband, before we were married.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:22.910
My husband's shoulder bumped into a man
who was walking by very forcefully.

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:26.750
He suddenly punched my husband.

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:31.290
I tried to stop him, and he
pushed me away again and again.

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:37.500
I didn't mean to kill him.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:42.790
I just wanted to get that brutal man
away from my husband.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:45.910
I've nearly turned myself in so many times!

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:49.750
But then, my husband and
I decided to get married...

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:51.200
I'm sorry.

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:56.450
Sorry that I wasn't able to apologize
to you this way for five whole years.

00:20:56.450 --> 00:21:00.370
I truly... I truly am sorry!

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:03.290
We realize how selfish this is of us.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:07.370
But next month is our baby's
expected delivery date.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:11.080
So please, give us just a bit more time.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.950
After that, we'll turn ourselves in.

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:18.080
Matsuoka-san, was it?

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:21.370
Tell me, are you two's
parents still alive and well?

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:22.700
Y-Yes.

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:24.120
Yes.

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:26.620
I see, I see.

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:32.700
With a baby on the way, we can't
exactly have the mother behind bars.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:39.040
Toshihiro, I'm sorry I'm such a fool of a dad.

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:46.200
In the end, I failed to raise you well,
or get revenge for you.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:52.870
Someday I'll come apologize in person,
so you just sit tight and calm down.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:05.830
This, this all ended for the best.

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:10.580
If I was your son...

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:14.580
...I'd be proud of you.
